    {"theme": "AI mega-rounds persist", "summary": "Supabase raised $500M at $10.5B (Series F, GIC-led), Helion $465M at $15.5B (Series G, Thrive Capital), Ramp $750M at $44B, Lila Sciences $2B at $8.5B autonomous labs, Suno $400M at $5.4B AI music."},
    {"theme": "Defense-tech investment boom", "summary": "Allen Control Systems raised $200M at $2.2B (autonomous turrets), Mach Industries $300M at $1.8B (Series C, Infinite/Ribbit). Motorola acquired Israeli counter-drone maker D-Fend Solutions for $1.5B."},
    {"theme": "US Government considering AI equity stakes ('AI USA Inc.')", "summary": "Senior US officials held talks about the government acquiring equity stakes in major AI companies such as OpenAI, with returns potentially paid as a public dividend — echoing proposals from both the Trump White House and Sen. Bernie Sanders."},
    {"theme": "Berkshire's first post-Buffett major acquisition", "summary": "Under new CEO Greg Abel, Berkshire agreed to acquire homebuilder Taylor Morrison Home for $6.8B in cash (24% premium), planning to merge it with Clayton Homes into a unified platform."},
    {"theme": "Benchmark strategy shift", "summary": "Benchmark effectively closed two new funds: a $750M 12th flagship (nearly doubling its longtime ~$425M size) and a $1.25B first-ever growth fund, driven by deal size inflation and its Cerebras SPV experience."},
    {"theme": "IPO market heats up: Quantinuum, Innio, Liftoff priced", "summary": "Quantinuum (quantum computing, Honeywell spinout) priced at $60/share, raising $1.68B at $15.56B valuation. Innio (German gas engines) raised $2.4B at $20.3B. Liftoff Mobile priced at $23 (above range), raising $437M."},
    {"theme": "MLB franchise valuations surge; pro sports PE dealmaking", "summary": "Padres sold for record $3.9B; Giants 10% stake to Sixth Street at $3.8B implied valuation. MLBs proposed salary cap/floor ahead of 2027 labor CBA."}
